    "route": "/practice-areas/small-claims-court-matters",
    "status": "draft",
    "source": "content/phase-1/practice-areas/small-claims-court-matters.md",
    "h1": "Small Claims Court paralegal services in Scarborough, Toronto.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Small Claims Court Matters",
        "depth": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "You may be owed money, disagree about a contract, or have received a claim you need to answer. Before deciding how to proceed, understand what the dispute is about, what evidence you have, and which dates need attention."
          },
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "{{business.name}} lists Small Claims Court matters among its practice areas. Contact the office to discuss making or defending a claim and the work you may need help with."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What you can ask about",
        "depth": 2,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "- Reviewing a potential claim or a claim served on you.\n- Preparing claims and defences.\n- Organizing contracts, invoices, messages, and payment records.\n- Preparing for a settlement conference.\n- Representation at trial within the agreed retainer.\n- Available steps to enforce a judgment."
          },
          {
            "kind": "editorial",
            "markdown": "Editorial note: Client to approve the accepted dispute types and enforcement services. Do not promise collection or recovery."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Is Small Claims Court the right place?",
        "depth": 2,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "Ontario Small Claims Court currently hears eligible claims for money or the return of personal property valued at $50,000 or less. The monetary limit increased on October 1, 2025. Being within the limit does not, by itself, establish that the court is the correct forum for every dispute."
          },
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "If your concern involves another tribunal, a different kind of remedy, or a larger claim, discuss the appropriate process before filing. Do not give up part of a claim merely to fit a limit without understanding the consequences."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Prepare the facts and documents",
        "depth": 2,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "Write down who the dispute involves, what was agreed, what happened, and what result you are seeking. Collect supporting records in date order. Include documents that do not support your position as well as those that do; an assessment needs the full picture."
          },
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "If you were served with a claim, keep the complete package and note when and how you received it. Seek advice about the response requirements promptly. Sending {{business.shortName}} an inquiry does not file a defence or stop the court process."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Proposed approach",
        "depth": 2,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "1. Identify the dispute, parties, amount, and relevant dates.\n2. Review the evidence and discuss the available process and practical costs.\n3. Agree on the proposed work and fees if the practice accepts the matter.\n4. Prepare for the agreed steps, which may include pleadings, settlement, trial, or enforcement."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Questions",
        "depth": 2,
        "blocks": []
      },
      {
        "heading": "Can you help if I am being sued?",
        "depth": 3,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "Ask about defence services and provide the response date immediately. Acceptance depends on the matter, availability, and any conflict of interest."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Does winning mean I will receive the money immediately?",
        "depth": 3,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "No. A judgment and collecting payment are separate matters. Enforcement may require further steps, costs, and an assessment of what is practical."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Will my dispute go to trial?",
        "depth": 3,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "Not every dispute does. Settlement may be discussed, but neither settlement nor a particular court outcome can be promised."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Discuss your claim or defence",
        "depth": 2,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "CTA: Request a Consultation → `/contact`"
          },
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "Call {{phone.primary}} or {{phone.office}}. {{address.full}}."
          },
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "Related: Employment matters → `/practice-areas/employment-human-rights-matters`; Landlord and tenant matters → `/practice-areas/landlord-tenant-matters`."
          },
          {
            "kind": "copy",
            "markdown": "General information only. The appropriate forum and response depend on your circumstances."
          },
          {
            "kind": "editorial",
            "markdown": "Research: Source S1 in `08-sources.md` for the current monetary limit. Reverify before publication."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Can you help if I am being sued?",
        "answer": "Ask about defence services and provide the response date immediately. Acceptance depends on the matter, availability, and any conflict of interest."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does winning mean I will receive the money immediately?",
        "answer": "No. A judgment and collecting payment are separate matters. Enforcement may require further steps, costs, and an assessment of what is practical."
      },
      {
        "question": "Will my dispute go to trial?",
        "answer": "Not every dispute does. Settlement may be discussed, but neither settlement nor a particular court outcome can be promised."
      }
    ],
